  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1221 AM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nSaturday through Thursday:\n\nThe frontal boundary will continue southward on Saturday, moving\nfairly slowly as it goes. Even though light winds will come\naround to northerly Saturday, humidity will remain, and highs\nwill be in the low to mid 80s. Surface pressure is expected to\nincrease through the day, and with the front retreating south,\nrain chances are not expected. High pressure will then linger\nSunday through Monday keeping us dry. Dew points will remain\nsomewhat elevated through the weekend as we will fail to get a\npush of appreciable dry air into southern WI, though highs will\ndip into upper 70s to low 80s. Warm advection then returns\nTuesday with increased chances for more thunderstorms with the\nNBM painting 25 to 50% PoPs over the area. Shower and storm\nchances then continue through the rest of the extended. CMiller",
